torage policy and declared attestation/user-verification/trust/custody evidence. Accepted fixture: Register credentials with fresh challenge, RP/origin/consent/storage policy and explicit attestation trust, presence/verification, backup/sync and custody assumptions. Negative fixture: Reject undeclared trust roots, treating synced passkeys as device-bound and attestation tracking beyond privacy policy. Required evidence: registration transcript, WebAuthn/passkey manifest and privacy/replay fixtures; bind source/compiler/profile/target/provider identities, source-mapped stable diagnostics and every applicable source facet field/exception/negative condition listed for this criterion in [the full preserved source context](#wider-integration-task-proposals). Dependencies consume auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/enforce-grant-intersection-attenuation-revocation-phase-and-lifetime, legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-safe-code-classification-and-taintunsafe-boundaries outputs under their stated contracts; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Status: Open; implementation acceptance unassessed.\n\nCriterion `domain/protected-disclosure-boundary`: Require explicit authorized audited encrypt/decrypt/reveal/reconstruct/attest/compare/branch/serialize/prompt/log/export boundaries with declared leakage/reveal policy. Accepted fixture: Authorize and audit encrypt/decrypt/reveal/reconstruct/attest/compare/branch/serialize/prompt/log/export operations with explicit reveal reason, participants and leakage state. Negative fixture: Reject implicit crossings, unsupported plaintext/ciphertext mixing and disclosures beyond declared output/metadata/timing/transcript policy. Required evidence: protected-boundary manifest and leakage/disclosure fixtures; bind source/compiler/profile/target/provider identities, source-mapped stable diagnostics and every applicable source facet field/exception/negative condition listed for this criterion in [the full preserved source context