ls, unbounded exceptions unless explicitly modeled, and ungranted privileged operations. Required outputs: Kernel profile/capability/memory/map/allocator/no-hidden-allocation and unsafe reports, legal provider fixtures and P7-HIDDEN-ALLOC/GC/RAW-MEMORY/EXCEPTION/AUTHORITY diagnostics. Dependencies: legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks, runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-memory-concurrency-and-typed-ffi-boundaries, auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/enforce-grant-intersection-attenuation-revocation-phase-and-lifetime interface facts, not whole-task completion. Exact source predicates and frozen evidence: [the preserved profile-interface context](plan.md#platform-source-context), mapping kernel/profile-memory-contract; all attached contextual and negative predicates remain required. No implementation acceptance is inferred. For this target, the architecture owner records the concrete target/ABI, accepted artifact kind, named simulator/device evidence and required service set before implementation scope is claimed. Reject a scope claim missing any required selection or incompatible with the declared profile; no target or product is selected by this task. Target integration consumes the exact Lower/Emit artifact and explicit runtime or no-runtime manifest plus required standard-library adapters. Record actual simulation/execution and applicable layout, clock, interrupt, unsafe-island, grant and source-to-artifact provenance checks; reject forbidden services, missing adapters, unauditable authority or a record-only execution claim. These target gates do not require completion of the full Platform Product.. Criterion `domain/kernel-artifact-production`: Produce source-linked kernel artifact, unsafe audit/capability manifests and emulator smoke evidence for the declared kernel slice. Accepted fixture: Emit the declared kernel object/boot image with syscall/interrupt tables, ABI, unsafe-audit, capability an