alidation/taint, capabilities and error translation through audited privileged wrappers. Negative fixture: Reject schema-less/taint-unsafe entry, unaudited raw memory and ambient authority. Required evidence: kernel ABI/syscall schema, wrapper audit and boundary fixtures; bind source/compiler/profile/target/provider identities, source-mapped stable diagnostics and every applicable source facet field/exception/negative condition listed for this criterion in [the full preserved Domain context](plan.md#platform-source-context). Dependencies consume backend-llvm, legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-ownership-borrow-initialization-and-lifetime-analysis outputs under their stated contracts; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Status: Open; implementation acceptance unassessed.\n\nSource basis: [Kernel contract](../../docs/phase-09-domain-specific-computing-coverage/126-dom3-operating-system-and-kernel-domain-specification.md)\n\nHistorical project paragraph (unchanged):\n<!-- platform-kernel-parent:end -->\n\nDeclared completion and remaining work: Adopt kernel ABI/execution model; implement initialization, memory and scheduling interface slice required by contract; verify unsafe boundaries, no hidden hosted services and artifact provenance\n\nSource basis: [Kernel contract](../../docs/phase-09-domain-specific-computing-coverage/126-dom3-operating-system-and-kernel-domain-specification.md)",
