unds, omitted temporal assumptions and stronger use-after-free requirements unsupported by the actual target or separate proof. Required outputs: Temporal/compartment assumption manifest, no-revocation acceptance and stronger-required rejection/proof cases, P8-TEMPORAL diagnostic identifying failed assumption and origin. Dependencies: legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks, backend-hdl interface facts, not whole-task completion. Exact source predicates and frozen evidence: [the preserved profile-interface context](plan.md#platform-source-context), mapping hardware/temporal-protection; all attached contextual and negative predicates remain required. No implementation acceptance is inferred. For this target, the architecture owner records the concrete target/ABI, accepted artifact kind, named simulator/device evidence and required service set before implementation scope is claimed. Reject a scope claim missing any required selection or incompatible with the declared profile; no target or product is selected by this task. Target integration consumes the exact Lower/Emit artifact and explicit runtime or no-runtime manifest plus required standard-library adapters. Record actual simulation/execution and applicable layout, clock, interrupt, unsafe-island, grant and source-to-artifact provenance checks; reject forbidden services, missing adapters, unauditable authority or a record-only execution claim. These target gates do not require completion of the full Platform Product.. Criterion `domain/hardware-fifo-integration`: Demonstrate the declared FIFO slice including full/empty/reset/backpressure/data-order behavior and absence of forbidden runtime services. Accepted fixture: Simulate the FIFO full, empty, reset, backpressure and data-order cases using fixed shapes, declared clocks and ready/valid interfaces. Negative fixture: Reject heap/host IO/dynamic dispatch, nonfinite control and missing CDC/timing evidence. Required evidence: HDL, testbench, interface/timing/source maps and simulation trace; bind source/compiler/profile/target/provider identities, source-mapped stable diagnostics and every applicable source facet field/exception/negative condition listed for this criterion in [the full preserved Domain context](plan.md#platform-source-context). Dependencies consume backend-hdl, legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks outputs under their stated contracts; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Status: Open; implementation acceptance unassessed. Criterion `domain/hardware-hdl-emission`: Emit traceable HDL, interface/clock/reset/timing records and executable simulation/testbench artifacts for accepted hardware IR. Accepted fixture: Emit HDL and source maps from accepted hardware IR together with interface, clock/reset/timing and simulation/testbench artifacts. Negative fixture: Reject an artifact missing source maps, typed vendor-IP boundary, timing constraints or simulation/equivalence evidence. Required evidence: traceable HDL artifact pack and conformance report; bind source/compiler/profile/target/provider identities, source-mapped stable diagnostics and every applicable source facet field/exception/negative condition listed for this criterion in [the full preserved Domain context](plan.md#platform-source-context). Dependencies consume backend-hdl, legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks outputs under their stated contracts; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Status: Open; implementation acceptance unassessed. Criterion `domain/hardware-shape-lowering`: Lower typed fixed-shape hardware values/control to finite hardware/domain IR, rejecting implicit widths/truncation and nonfinite runtime-only operations. Accepted fixture: Lower fixed-width/signed/shape signals, registers, ports, buses, memories and finite state/control under declared clock/reset/layout and truncation contracts. Negative fixture: Reject implicit host widths, undeclared truncation, software-pointer/runtime dependencies and control that cannot become finite hardware. Required evidence: finite hardware IR, shape/clock/reset records and rejected-source diagnostics; bind source/compiler/profile/target/provider identities, source-mapped stable diagnostics and every applicable source facet field/exception/negative condition listed for this criterion in [the full preserved Domain context](plan.md#platform-source-context). Dependencies consume backend-hdl, legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks outputs under their stated contracts; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Status: Open; implementation acceptance unassessed.\n\nSource basis: [Hardware contract](../../docs/phase-09-domain-specific-computing-coverage/124-dom1-hardware-computing-domain-specification.md)\n\nHistorical project paragraph (unchanged):\n<!-- platform-hardware-parent:end -->\n\nDeclared completion and remaining work: Adopt clock/reset/HDL target contract; implement state-machine lowering and simulation; verify timing/reset invariants and reject illegal dynamic/runtime operations; emit traceable hardware artifact\n\nSource basis: [Hardware contract](../../docs/phase-09-domain-specific-computing-coverage/124-dom1-hardware-computing-domain-specification.md)",
