  "- [ ] `evolution/security-review` Perform and record evidence-backed security review\n\nStatus: Open\n\nSource requirement: `governance/security-review`\n\nRequired outputs: Threat model, review scope, evidence, decision, residual risk and accepted mitigations Release-preserved security review references and applicable exception/advisory links\n\nClosing evidence: Before accepting authority/secret/taint/unsafe/FFI/plugin/host/AI/package changes, review actual trust boundaries and source evidence, not only metadata presence. Capability review includes least privilege/denial/redaction; secrets include lifetime/memory/serialization/retention; taint includes propagation/validation/sinks; unsafe/FFI/host/plugin changes include audit/boundary tests. AI review includes prompt-injection probes, tool authorization, ai/human-review and eval gates; supply-chain review includes identity/provenance/signature/SBOM/dependency confusion/malware. Accountable governance explicitly disposes high residual risk. Actual complete accepted artifact and consumer result for the named source contract, with input/source/policy/tool identity. Historical stage0 records or a passing schema alone do not implement these outcomes. Criterion governance/unsafe-audit-decision: Produce a distinct GOV9 specialist unsafe-audit decision for the exact island/source/owner/profile/target/wrapper revision, preserving the difference from a GOV4 security decision. Review every pre/postcondition, invariant, proof/runtime check and declared effect/capability, memory/alias/lifetime/initialization/concurrency/FFI/backend assumption using actual SAFE6 records, wrapper evidence, invalid-precondition negatives and applicable fuzz/sanitizer/model/formal/optimization-preservation results. Require GOV3/STD20 for standard-library islands and GOV4 for security impact. Emit scoped audit/verdict, evidence and stale/revalidation record, with package/release unsafe provenance. Revalidate after relevant compiler/optimizer/bac