  "- [ ] `firmware` Firmware / `firmware`\n\nStatus: Open\n\n<!-- platform-firmware-parent:start -->\n### Firmware parent proposed criteria\n\nCurrent refinement of the same Open `firmware` target-conformance task.\nResume the full body from\n[the published reconciliation](https://github.com/burn2delete/uniform/blob/2c88b9796fc0d0e6ca0bdc93cbfba41cb6921dcc/specs/platform-workflow/tasks.md#implementation-tasks).\nOnly profile/Domain context references change; other proposed text and the\noriginal short paragraph below remain preserved. Existing target maintainers\nretain ownership; no person, target/ABI, device or product is adopted here.\nThe [composition plan](plan.md#target-conformance-and-product-composition)\nkeeps Types/Legality/Auth checks, domain IR, Lower/Emit/backend products,\nactual Runtime/provider calls and target evidence distinct. A target slice\nis not the full Platform Product and does not receive acceptance by linking\nsource criteria. Current source/owner repartition and review remain pending.\n\nDeclared completion and remaining work: Adopt device memory/startup target; implement interrupt/MMIO/startup and explicit allocation; verify image/link map and rejected unsupported services on execution or named emulator. DOM2 acceptance requires memory map, startup/reset, interrupt vectors, stack/static-allocation/section and panic/BSP records; typed volatile/ordered/capability-checked MMIO and audited wrappers; declared interrupt effects and synchronization. Exercise timer sensor reset/acknowledgement/buffer/panic behavior and UART, reject hidden hosted services and unauthorized MMIO, and emit image/link/source/audit maps with boot/simulator evidence. Dependencies: profile legality, native lowering and runtime memory/startup boundaries; physical memory representability remains separate from removed project accounting ; P6 target conformance requires explicit stack/static/region/arena/provider capacity/reset/failure policy and no hidden GC/host services; unknown stack use rejects in strict mode. Check device-map address/width/alignment/volatility/order/grants, interrupt source/priority/shared-state/atomic/reentrancy/stack/latency/context, and required physical loop/recursion/blocking-timeout evidence; missing evidence rejects or requires the policy-permitted unsafe audit. Reject invalid maps, missing device authority, host calls and unbounded handler behavior. Emit image/linker/memory/device/vector/interrupt/latency/safety manifests with source provenance. Physical memory/timing requirements are not compiler work allowances; product target choice remains unassessed Foundation requirement gravity/realtime-not-throughput-proof: For a realtime claim record the declared deadline and worst-case execution/latency/jitter assumptions, target, interference, allocation/blocking/interrupt policy and applicable analysis or measurement evidence; retain throughput benchmarks as a different evidence class. Refusals: Reject deadline guarantees inferred from mean throughput, a different target/load, missing worst-case assumptions or hidden blocking/allocation; physical timing constraints are not compiler work quotas. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-explicit-family-selection-and-no-runtime-rejection - Selected runtime/provider service contracts and actual link/load/service-use evidence; pass-evidence - Actual subject-bound checker/proof/certificate/audit/replay/test evidence and verdicts.. Criterion profile-gap/firmware/device-mmio (Open): Input: Firmware source device operation and device map with base/register offsets, access direction, width, alignment, volatility, order and hardware capability. Accept: Admit typed MMIO only when the map, address/width/alignment/access, volatile/ordering rules and scope agree; require the declared typed wrapper or reviewed unsafe island for raw device operations. Reject: Absent or inconsistent device map, invalid address/width/alignment/access/order, missing device authority and raw address arithmetic presented as ordinary safe MMIO. Required outputs: MMIO/device map, wrapper/audit evidence and accepted/invalid-map/missing-grant diagnostics carrying target/device/region/span/generated-origin/effect/capability and missing proof. Dependencies: devices, legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks, auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/enforce-grant-intersection-attenuation-revocation-phase-and-lifetime interface facts, not whole-task completion. Exact source predicates and frozen evidence: [the preserved profile-interface context](plan.md#platform-source-context), mapping firmware/device-mmio; all attached contextual and negative predicates remain required. No implementation acceptance is inferred. Criterion profile-gap/firmware/interrupt-contract (Open): Input: Firmware interrupt handler with source/vector, priority, latency and stack requirements, capabilities, shared state, atomic/critical-section and reentrancy context. Accept: Validate handler authority, target context, stack/latency and shared-state safety; preserve declared priority, reentrancy and synchronization; permit only the declared bounded provider/context behavior. Reject: Unbounded allocation or indefinite blocking, host services, invalid captures, missing interrupt authority, invalid shared-state/atomic discipline or unsatisfied required stack/latency evidence. Required outputs: Interrupt capability/vector table, stack/latency/shared-state report, handler acceptance/rejection fixtures and P6-INTERRUPT/P6-CAPABILITY or relevant proof diagnostic with origin/context. Dependencies: devices, legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks, auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/enforce-grant-intersection-attenuation-revocation-phase-and-lifetime interface facts, not whole-task completion. Exact source predicates and frozen evidence: [the preserved profile-interface context](plan.md#platform-source-context), mapping firmware/interrupt-contract; all attached contextual and negative predicates remain required. No implementation acceptance is inferred. Criterion profile-gap/firmware/physical-timing-contract (Open): Input: Firmware call graph and realtime-affecting loops, recursion, stack, interrupts, blocking and allocation under explicit physical target policy. Accept: Check required loop/recursion/worst-case stack/interrupt-latency/blocking-timeout/allocation evidence against actual declared physical constraints; unknown stack rejects in strict mode; missing evidence rejects or follows only the explicitly permitted unsafe-audit policy. Reject: Missing/exceeded physical evidence, indefinite blocking and hidden runtime assumptions; never substitute compiler work counters or fabricated project allowances for physical timing proof. Required outputs: Loop/latency/stack/allocation constraint and proof report with target/span/generated-origin/device/interrupt/required-bound information and accepted/rejected/conditional-audit cases. Dependencies: legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks, lower/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/lower1-validate-lowering-inputs interface facts, not whole-task completion. Exact source predicates and frozen evidence: [the preserved profile-interface context](plan.md#platform-source-context), mapping firmware/physical-timing-contract; all attached contextual and negative predicates remain required. No implementation acceptance is inferred. Criterion profile-gap/firmware/profile-memory-contract (Open): Input: Firmware namespace/call graph and stack/static/region/arena or explicitly permitted bounded provider, image/linker/memory/vector/device c