ore implementation scope is claimed. Reject a scope claim missing any required selection or incompatible with the declared profile; no target or product is selected by this task. Target integration consumes the exact Lower/Emit artifact and explicit runtime or no-runtime manifest plus required standard-library adapters. Record actual simulation/execution and applicable layout, clock, interrupt, unsafe-island, grant and source-to-artifact provenance checks; reject forbidden services, missing adapters, unauditable authority or a record-only execution claim. These target gates do not require completion of the full Platform Product.. Criterion `domain/device-adaptation`: Expose vendor/hosted/mobile device APIs through typed permission/lifecycle/thread/null/error/taint adapters. Accepted fixture: Invoke typed hosted/mobile/vendor device adapters with permission, lifecycle, thread/actor, null/error and taint contracts. Negative fixture: Reject missing permissions, lifecycle/thread violations, unchecked nulls or a vendor call presented as safe without a boundary. Required evidence: device adapter manifest and permission/lifecycle/error fixtures; bind source/compiler/profile/target/provider identities, source-mapped stable diagnostics and every applicable source facet field/exception/negative condition listed for this criterion in [the full preserved Domain context](plan.md#platform-source-context). Dependencies consume runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-memory-concurrency-and-typed-ffi-boundaries, auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/enforce-grant-intersection-attenuation-revocation-phase-and-lifetime outputs under their stated contracts; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Status: Open; implementation acceptance unassessed. Criterion `domain/device-uart-integration`: Execute the declared UART driver slice with register/DMA/interrupt evidence and denied unauthorized/unsafe accesses. Accepted fixture: Run UART transmit/receive/overflow/interrupt acknowledgement with register, DMA, lifetime and synchronization records. Negative fixture: Reject unauthorized MMIO, invalid DMA lifetime or interrupt cleanup/effect violations. Required evidence: register/MMIO/DMA manifests and simulator/device trace; bind source/compiler/profile/target/provider identities, source-mapped stable diagnostics and every applicable source facet field/exception/negative condition listed for this criterion in [the full preserved Domain context](plan.md#platform-source-context). Dependencies consume runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-memory-concurrency-and-typed-ffi-boundaries, auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/enforce-grant-intersection-attenuation-revocation-phase-and-lifetime outputs under their stated contracts; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Status: Open; implementation acceptance unassessed. Criterion `domain/typed-mmio`: Perform register/MMIO access under explicit address/width/alignment/endian/volatile/ordering/authority and audited-wrapper contracts. Accepted fixture: Validate register address, width, alignment, endian, volatile and ordering behavior with explicit authority and unsafe/audited safe-wrapper contracts. Negative fixture: Reject untyped, nonvolatile, misaligned, unordered or ungranted MMIO access. Required evidence: register schema, MMIO audit and register-access fixtures; bind source/compiler/profile/target/provider identities, source-mapped stable diagnostics and every applicable source facet field/exception/negative condition listed for this criterion in [the full preserved Domain context](plan.md#platform-source-context). Dependencies consume runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-memory-concurrency-and-typed-ffi-boundaries, auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/enforce-grant-intersection-attenuation-revocation-phase-and-lifetime outputs under their stated contracts; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Status: Open; implementation acceptance unassessed.\n\nSource basis: [Device contract](