  "- [ ] `release/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/execute-runtime-conformance-fixtures` Execute runtime conformance fixtures\n\nStatus: Open\n\nEvidence baseline: [TEST3](../../docs/phase-14-testing-verification-and-conformance/192-test3-runtime-test-strategy.md)\n\nClosing evidence: Implement and execute the Execute runtime conformance fixtures runner against actual declared owner interfaces, retaining the exact implementation/compiler/source/fixture/profile/target and applicable runtime/backend/provider identities. Run the named passing and failing cases; missing evidence is failure for the claimed scope, while inapplicable cases are explicitly reported. Source testing/test3/ai-ledger: Test and reconstruct runtime model/prompt/tool/memory/policy/human-review/replay events using model/tool ledgers. Concrete acceptance: Run model/tool/memory/policy/review/replay fixtures and delete or alter one causal ledger event; reconstruction must fail and unauthorized operations must remain denied. Retain actual input/output and diagnostic identities plus positive and rejected-case artifacts; supplied success flags, proposal delivery and broad parent links are not executable evidence. Source testing/test3/capability-denial: Deny runtime operations with missing grants and execute fixtures without ambient host services or authority. Concrete acceptance: Exercise the same runtime operation with its exact grant and with absent, narrowed or revoked grants; observe denial before the side effect and reject ambient authority. Retain actual input/output and diagnostic identities plus positive and rejected-case artifacts; supplied success flags, proposal delivery and broad parent links are not executable evidence. Source testing/test3/concurrency: Test runtime scheduling, synchronization, actors and race-prevention claims. Concrete acceptance: Exercise scheduler, synchronization, actors and supported race-prevention claims; inject an invalid synchronization or ownership edge and require the