  "- [ ] `release/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/execute-performance-regression-fixtures` Execute performance regression fixtures\n\nStatus: Open\n\nEvidence baseline: [TEST12](../../docs/phase-14-testing-verification-and-conformance/201-test12-performance-regression-test-plan.md)\n\nClosing evidence: Implement and execute the Execute performance regression fixtures runner against actual declared owner interfaces, retaining the exact implementation/compiler/source/fixture/profile/target and applicable runtime/backend/provider identities. Run the named passing and failing cases; missing evidence is failure for the claimed scope, while inapplicable cases are explicitly reported. Source testing/test12/ai-costs: Separate actual AI provider/model, tool, memory, human-review and replay costs/latencies instead of collapsing provider/tool latency into an opaque number. Concrete acceptance: Measure provider/model, tool, memory, human-review and replay cost/latency separately; reject an opaque collapsed total or identities not tied to actual observations. External costs do not impose compiler work quotas. Retain actual input/output and diagnostic identities plus positive and rejected-case artifacts; supplied success flags, proposal delivery and broad parent links are not executable evidence. Source testing/test12/device-counters: Declare device/counter source and reject counters unavailable on the declared target/device. Concrete acceptance: Collect a supported device counter with device and source identity, then request an unavailable/mismatched counter; reject the unsupported measurement rather than fabricating a sample. Retain actual input/output and diagnostic identities plus positive and rejected-case artifacts; supplied success flags, proposal delivery and broad parent links are not executable evidence. Source testing/test12/report: Emit benchmark manifest, raw measurements, summary/comparison reports, regression decision, semantic gate report and safety evidence links. C