  "- [ ] `release/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/produce-actual-self-hosted-compilerruntime-execution` Produce actual self-hosted compiler/runtime execution\n\nStatus: Open\n\nEvidence baseline: [Binary release status](../../docs/phase-18-binary-distribution-and-seedless-release/README.md)\n\n<!-- release-parent-self-hosting:start -->\nAdditional proposed source criteria (Open), from the published Release\n[task source](https://github.com/burn2delete/uniform/blob/df11890b21f71d3f246cc47e9f63d866239a0d68/specs/release-workflow/tasks.md).\nThe following closing-evidence text is preserved verbatim; the original\ncriterion below and existing governance interfaces remain required.\n\nActually invoke the prior Gravity compiler process on the complete declared next-stage compiler/runtime/library/build closure, retain real outputs and logs/lineage, link/package and execute that next compiler on accepted and rejected compiler inputs without Clojure in candidate compilation/runtime/build; then public check/run/compile and output executable demonstrate absent seed boundaries. SH25 component construction, SH27 equivalence and final release acceptance remain distinct; supplied rebuild records or plans do not prove execution. Release extension release/selfhosted-artifact-production: Produce the final public gravity executable through the actual stage3/self-hosted compiler and emitter, retaining compiler/backend/runtime/release-compiler paths, source/debug maps, executable hashes and provenance for the required compiler/runtime/library/build closure. Reject Clojure packaging with P18T03001 and retain P18T03002-P18T03004 blockers while retirement or path evidence is incomplete. A candidate manifest does not prove executable production. Release extension release/seed-boundary-exclusion: Prove Clojure is outside every required final boundary: public binary, compiler path, runtime path and release-compiler path, including required library/package/build closure. Bind proof, TCB delta, eligibility and provenance to actual artifacts; keep gravity-bootstrap explicit and excluded as recovery. Reject missing seed facts, regression, bootstrap confusion and compiler ambiguity. Clojure in any required boundary fails P18T05001; incomplete retirement retains P18T05003 as applicable. Release extension release/selfhosted-full-language-conformance: Pass final gravity test or an explicitly accepted equivalent full-language runner through the actual self-hosted public binary for the declared final surface. Retain binary/compiler hashes, command transcripts, applicable suites, positive/rejected cases and results. Reject hosted subset substitution, missing/failed suites and internal runner substitution. Inherited stage receipts and counters alone cannot prove this final boundary. Release extension release/successful-selfhost-verification: Succeed at final gravity self-host verify or its explicitly accepted equivalent through the exact self-hosted public binary. Final proof records :clojure-seed-boundary? false with actual source/compiler/runtime/release lineage. Exercise final success and refuse missing, stale, mismatched or active-seed proof inputs. The hosted incomplete P18T04007 surface remains refusal history, never final success.\n<!-- release-parent-self-hosting:end -->\n\nClosing evidence: Actually invoke the prior Gravity compiler process on the complete declared next-stage compiler/runtime/library/build closure, retain real outputs and logs/lineage, link/package and execute that next compiler on accepted and rejected compiler inputs without Clojure in candidate compilation/runtime/build; then public check/run/compile and output executable demonstrate absent seed boundaries. SH25 component construction, SH27 equivalence and final release acceptance remain distinct; supplied rebuild records or plans do not prove execution.",
